          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Brought up something that looked like old coffee grounds this morning after a night of retching.",
          "answer": "You should call for emergency medical help immediately. Vomiting material that looks like coffee grounds can be a sign of gastrointestinal bleeding, which requires urgent medical attention, as stated in the Gastroenterology and emergency medicine society guidance on gastrointestinal bleeding.\n\nVomit that resembles old coffee grounds typically indicates the presence of digested blood. This appearance is due to blood interacting with stomach acid. A clinician would investigate to find the source of this bleeding, which commonly occurs in the upper part of the digestive tract.\n\nWhile retching can have various causes, the presence of coffee-ground-like material in your vomit is the most important symptom and should be assessed by medical professionals without delay.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
